        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Interbol\n- Organizations: Russian Space Agency, Space Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences\n- Concepts: Plasma, states of matter\n- People: Irving Langmuir\n- Topics: Plasma physics\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1920s, chemist Irving Langmuir first introduced plasma as a concept.\n- Interbol is an international space project led by the Russian Space Agency and the Space Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences.\n- Plasma is a gaseous mixture of negatively charged electrons and highly charged positive ions.\n- Plasma production involves a distinct separation of ions and electrons that creates an electric field, which produces electric currents and magnetic fields.\n- Plasma is one of the four fundamental states of matter.",
